<header><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/pull/391">Sports Edge Lab <span> · College football</span></a><span>V096 actual return<br>V097 continuation review</span></header>
<div id="error" class="error" role="alert" hidden></div>
<main id="report" hidden>
<nav aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#actual">Actual work</a><a href="#cpu">CPU evidence</a><a href="#leaders">Selected results</a><a href="#sources">Market coverage</a><a href="#next">Next work</a><a href="#custody">Verified custody</a></nav>
<div class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Verified progress · Remaining scientific work</p><h1>The test campaign finished.<br>The wider program is still partial.</h1><p class="lead">V096 completed its registered campaign and published a verified resumable return. It added 312 model fits and reused all 624 completed validation jobs. Broader source, horizon and feature work remains unfinished.</p></div><aside class="status"><p class="eyebrow">Observed child and supervisor exit 0</p><h3>Operationally finished.<br>Scientifically partial.</h3><p id="closure-note"></p></aside></div>
<div class="metrics"><article class="metric"><span>New model fits</span><strong id="new-fits"></strong><p>Plus 312 calibrator fits. Zero failed fits.</p></article><article class="metric"><span>Registered jobs completed</span><strong id="complete-jobs"></strong><p>624 reused validation jobs + 312 test jobs.</p></article><article class="metric"><span>Actual fit processes</span><strong id="fit-processes"></strong><p>17 simultaneous fits within the 24-worker ceiling.</p></article><article class="metric"><span>Known completed test games</span><strong id="test-games"></strong><p>All 1,105 policies score the known 755-game population.</p></article></div>
<div class="notice warn">The latest invocation is not an operational crash. Its wider scientific result remains incomplete: official and postseason census completeness is unproven, upcoming feature rows are missing, and the full V13 program is not finished. Both outcomes remain explicit.</div>
<section id="actual"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Actual owner execution</p><h2>Completed work stays completed</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Invocation and tally</h3><dl class="facts" id="actual-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="actual-clock"></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Prediction rows have their own scope</h3><dl class="facts" id="prediction-facts"></dl><p class="fine">Inventory totals include reused predictions and rescoring. Newly materialized blend rows are not all novel forecasts. These row counts are not unique-game counts or claims of original live issuance.</p></article></div><article class="card" style="margin-top:18px"><h3>The finished finite campaign</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Branch</th><th scope="col" class="num">Completed</th><th scope="col" class="num">Reused</th><th scope="col" class="num">New models</th><th scope="col" class="num">New calibrators</th></tr></thead><tbody id="branch-rows"></tbody></table></div></article></section>
<section id="cpu"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Measured throughput</p><h2>The fitting phase used multiple cores. Scoring remained serial.</h2><p class="muted">The same invocation can show a busy fitting pool and later spend minutes near one core. The measurements below keep worker count, CPU seconds, elapsed time and acceptance windows separate.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Average CPU-equivalent during each phase</h3><div id="phase-bars"></div><div class="legend"><span>Optimizer</span><span class="prep">Preparation</span><span class="other">Other callback work</span><span class="serial">Serial scoring</span></div><p class="fine">Derived as recorded process CPU seconds divided by that phase's elapsed seconds, on a common 24-core scale. It is an average, not a count of simultaneously active processes. The fit bar sums worker phases only.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>A real three-minute window passed</h3><dl class="facts" id="gate-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="gate-limit"></p></article></div><article class="card" style="margin-top:18px"><div class="grid"><div><h3>Measured phase accounting</h3><dl class="facts" id="phase-facts"></dl></div><div><h3>Queue and full-host cost</h3><dl class="facts" id="queue-facts"></dl><p class="fine" id="queue-definition"></p></div></div></article><div class="notice" id="cpu-action"></div></section>
<section id="leaders"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Validation selects · 2026 reports</p><h2>Nine T-120 leaders, now scored on the known test population</h2><p class="muted">At the 120-minute pregame horizon, every displayed contender has 919/919 eligible completed games in 2024, 934/934 in 2025 and 755/755 in the observed 2026 test population. One additional archived 2024 row remains ungraded. Original issued forecasts and these exposed frozen reconstructions are separate evidence classes.</p><div class="controls"><label>Annual validation weights<select id="profile" aria-label="Annual validation weights"><option value="50/50">50/50 · primary</option><option value="40/60">40/60 · sensitivity</option><option value="30/70">30/70 · sensitivity</option><option value="20/80">20/80 · sensitivity</option><option value="10/90">10/90 · sensitivity</option></select></label><button id="download" type="button">Download this evidence</button></div><p id="profile-note" class="fine" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="card"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="leader-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Objective</th><th scope="col">Saved policy</th><th scope="col" class="num">2024 · 919/919</th><th scope="col" class="num">2025 · 934/934</th><th scope="col" class="num">Validation score</th><th scope="col" class="num">2026 · 755/755</th></tr></thead><tbody id="leader-rows"></tbody></table></div></div><div class="notice warn">2026 outcomes did not select these policies. Changing the validation ratio reuses the same annual predictions; it does not refit estimators or reweight training rows. Prior test exposure remains disclosed. Complete coverage of the known population does not prove a complete official census, a pristine test set or production eligibility.</div><details><summary>How the primary leaders rank under each sensitivity ratio</summary><div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:15px"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Objective</th><th scope="col" class="num">50/50</th><th scope="col" class="num">40/60</th><th scope="col" class="num">30/70</th><th scope="col" class="num">20/80</th><th scope="col" class="num">10/90</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rank-rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="fine">These are the saved ranks of each 50/50 primary policy, not ranks chosen on 2026. The selector above shows the actual winner for each validation ratio.</p></details></section>
<section id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Source evidence and missing histories</p><h2>Reference coverage is not a predictive market benchmark</h2><p class="muted">DraftKings, native Kalshi, Polymarket Global and Polymarket US retain separate source routes. The controls display the T-120 completed-game coverage grid across all 18 recorded bookmakers/products. Zero means no qualified row in this grid; it is not an invented price or a conclusion about all possible source history.</p><div class="controls"><label>Season<select id="source-season" aria-label="Source coverage season"><option>2026</option><option>2025</option><option>2024</option></select></label><label>Target<select id="source-target" aria-label="Source coverage target"><option value="winner">Winner</option><option value="margin">Margin</option><option value="total">Total</option></select></label></div><div class="card"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="source-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Bookmaker / route</th><th scope="col" class="num">Qualified features</th><th scope="col" class="num">Original availability</th><th scope="col" class="num">Predictive baseline</th></tr></thead><tbody id="source-rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="fine" id="source-note"></p></div><div class="notice warn" id="exchange-note"></div></section>
<section id="next"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Finite continuation</p><h2>More research, with completed work preserved</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3 id="next-title">V097 preparation</h3><p id="next-status" class="policy-name"></p><dl class="facts" id="next-facts"></dl><p class="digest" id="next-digest"></p><p class="fine" id="summary-comparison"></p><p class="fine">A planned job is not a promised new fit. Exact completed checkpoints and fitted components are reused first. The owner launches the research command; preparing this report launches no owner work. The 24-worker native projection is rechecked at launch and is not measured V097 fit occupancy.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Known forecast coverage still has gaps</h3><dl class="facts" id="population-facts"></dl><p class="fine">All 397 retained policies were regraded without changing their original prediction values. The 133 pending-game denominator stays visible. The exact frozen contexts retain ten pending feature gaps per target.</p></article></div><article class="card" style="margin-top:18px"><h3>What remains outside the finished campaign</h3><div id="remaining-branches"></div></article></section>
<section id="custody"><p class="eyebrow">06 / Integrity, storage and publication</p><h2>A verified partial return can be resumed</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Actual storage accounting</h3><dl class="facts" id="storage-facts"></dl><p class="digest" id="return-digest"></p><p class="fine">The control ZIP is not the full scientific storage total. The 512 MiB limit applies to each transport part; it is not an aggregate science cap. Unchanged durable payloads remain verified references.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Source review only</h3><p>This report publishes bounded aggregates and coarse model groups. It omits private recipes, weights, source arrays, execution packages and complete candidate forecast grids.</p><p>GitHub source, hosted website deployment and production promotion are separate actions. This source review is unmerged and does not deploy a website or promote a model.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/fbs/v093-launch-readiness-20261117/docs/fbs/v093">Read the preserved V093/V095 history</a></p></article></div><details style="margin-top:18px"><summary>Evidence digests and their scope</summary><div id="evidence-pins"></div><p class="fine">The downloaded JSON is the exact bounded projection embedded in this report. Digests identify the inspected source artifacts; they do not grant access to private payloads or establish redistribution rights.</p></details></section>
</main><footer><p id="footer-note">This dated report is not a live process monitor. Research preparation creates no owner execution.</p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/pull/391">Review source</a></footer>
<script id="report-data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script>
<script>
'use strict';
(async()=>{
const raw=document.getElementById('report-data').textContent, expected='__DATA_SHA256__';
const digest=Array.from(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256',new TextEncoder().encode(raw)))).map(x=>x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');
if(digest!==expected)throw Error('The embedded evidence does not match this report. No result is displayed.');
const d=JSON.parse(raw);if(d.schema!=='fbs.public.actual-and-continuation.v097'||d.owner!=='FBS'||d.execution.scientific_complete!==false||d.selection.test_used_for_selection!==false||d.publication.website_deployed!==false)throw Error('Report scope is inconsistent.');
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id), text=(id,x)=>{$(id).textContent=x}, num=x=>x.toLocaleString('en-US'), sec=x=>x.toFixed(3)+' s', cpu=x=>x.toFixed(3)+' CPU-s', pct=x=>(100*x).toFixed(4)+'%', mib=x=>(x/1048576).toFixed(2)+' MiB', gb=x=>(x/1e9).toFixed(3)+' GB', clock=x=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US',{dateStyle:'medium',timeStyle:'short',timeZone:'America/Los_Angeles'}).format(new Date(x))+' Pacific';
const facts=(id,rows)=>{const target=$(id);target.replaceChildren();for(const [label,value]of rows){const row=document.createElement('div'),dt=document.createElement('dt'),dd=document.createElement('dd');dt.textContent=label;dd.textContent=String(value);row.append(dt,dd);target.append(row)}};
const cell=(row,label,value,cls='')=>{const td=document.createElement('td');td.dataset.label=label;td.className=cls;if(value instanceof Node)td.append(value);else td.textContent=String(value);row.append(td);return td};
const objective=(target,metric)=>target[0].toUpperCase()+target.slice(1)+' '+({accuracy:'accuracy',brier:'Brier',log_loss:'log loss',mae:'MAE',rmse:'RMSE',crps:'CRPS'}[metric]);
const metric=(value,kind)=>kind==='accuracy'?pct(value):value.toFixed(6);
const a=d.execution,c=d.cpu,s=d.selection,p=d.population,n=d.next_preparation;
text('closure-note','Supervisor closure observed '+clock(a.observed_at)+'. The verified return is partial and resumable. No production promotion is claimed.');text('new-fits',a.new_model_fits);text('complete-jobs',a.completed_jobs+' / '+a.registered_jobs);text('fit-processes',c.observed_fit_processes);text('test-games',p.completed_test_games);
facts('actual-facts',[['Child / supervisor exit','0 / 0'],['Return integrity','Verified'],['Full V13 science','Incomplete'],['Historical failed attempts',a.historical_failed_attempts],['Operationally finished attempts',a.operationally_finished_attempts],['Fully V13-complete attempts',a.fully_v13_complete_attempts]]);text('actual-clock',a.tally_scope+'. V096 is counted once as operationally finished with partial science. Its provisional child snapshot is superseded by the authenticated supervisor closure.');
facts('prediction-facts',[['New model-callback prediction rows',num(a.new_callback_prediction_rows)],['Materialized blend rows',num(a.materialized_blend_rows)],['Scored campaign inventory',num(a.scored_inventory_rows)],['Forecast inventory, including ungraded',num(a.forecast_inventory_rows)]]);
for(const x of a.branch_counts){const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Branch',x.label);for(const [label,key]of [['Completed','completed_jobs'],['Reused','checkpoint_reused_jobs'],['New models','new_model_fits'],['New calibrators','new_calibrator_fits']])cell(tr,label,x[key],'num');$('branch-rows').append(tr)}
const bar=(label,wall,values)=>{const phase=document.createElement('div');phase.className='phase';const head=document.createElement('div');head.className='phase-head';const l=document.createElement('span'),v=document.createElement('strong');l.textContent=label;const total=values.reduce((z,x)=>z+x[1],0)/wall;v.textContent=total.toFixed(2)+' cores';head.append(l,v);const track=document.createElement('div');track.className='bar-track';track.setAttribute('role','img');track.setAttribute('aria-label',label+': '+total.toFixed(3)+' average CPU-equivalent cores on a 24-core scale');for(const [kind,value]of values){const part=document.createElement('span');part.className='bar '+kind;part.style.width=(value/wall/c.hard_ceiling*100)+'%';track.append(part)}phase.append(head,track);$('phase-bars').append(phase)};
bar('Fit dispatch',c.dispatch_wall_seconds,[['fit',c.optimizer_cpu_seconds],['prepare',c.preparation_cpu_seconds],['other',c.other_callback_cpu_seconds]]);bar('Coordinator scoring',c.scoring_wall_seconds,[['serial',c.scoring_cpu_seconds]]);bar('Retained-policy grading',c.retained_scoring_wall_seconds,[['serial',c.retained_scoring_cpu_seconds]]);
facts('gate-facts',[['Required useful-work result',c.useful_gate_status],['Preparation + optimizer occupancy',pct(c.useful_gate_fraction)+' of '+c.useful_gate_workers],['Optimizer-only occupancy',pct(c.optimizer_gate_fraction)+' of '+c.useful_gate_workers],['Measured interval',sec(c.useful_gate_seconds)],['Model + calibrator completions',c.optimizer_completions_in_gate],['Final exhausted-queue status','Conditional, no work remaining']]);text('gate-limit','The saved earlier window passed. The final empty-queue observation remains '+c.end_queue_status+'; it does not erase the earlier pass. The 418 completions include calibrators and are not 418 new base models.');
facts('phase-facts',[['Fit dispatch elapsed',sec(c.dispatch_wall_seconds)],['Optimizer CPU',cpu(c.optimizer_cpu_seconds)],['Preparation CPU',cpu(c.preparation_cpu_seconds)],['Other worker callback CPU',cpu(c.other_callback_cpu_seconds)],['Coordinator scoring elapsed / CPU',sec(c.scoring_wall_seconds)+' / '+cpu(c.scoring_cpu_seconds)],['Retained grading elapsed / CPU',sec(c.retained_scoring_wall_seconds)+' / '+cpu(c.retained_scoring_cpu_seconds)]]);
facts('queue-facts',[['Prepared queue high watermark',c.prepared_queue_high_watermark],['Preparation pending with idle slots',sec(c.pending_preparation_with_idle_slots_seconds)],['Legacy preparation-not-ready measure',sec(c.legacy_preparation_not_ready_seconds)],['Whole supervised invocation',(c.whole_execution_wall_seconds/60).toFixed(2)+' min'],['Recorded full-host compute estimate','$'+d.cost.estimated_full_host_usd.toFixed(6)],['Compute guard','$'+d.cost.guard_usd]]);text('queue-definition','The legacy not-ready measure may include workers actively preparing; it is not pure starvation. The cost is an estimate through '+clock(d.cost.measured_at)+', not an invoice. Subphase costs must not be added to this whole-invocation estimate.');
text('cpu-action','The fit pool did use '+c.workers+' workers. Its '+(c.dispatch_wall_seconds/60).toFixed(2)+'-minute dispatch was only one phase of a '+(c.whole_execution_wall_seconds/60).toFixed(2)+'-minute invocation. Parallel, checkpointed grading is part of the prepared continuation; it has not yet demonstrated a new owner-run speedup.');
function renderLeaders(){const profile=$('profile').value;const rows=s.leaders.filter(x=>x.profile===profile);$('leader-rows').replaceChildren();for(const x of rows){const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Objective',objective(x.target,x.metric));const policy=document.createElement('span');policy.className='policy-name';policy.textContent=x.family;const sub=document.createElement('span');sub.className='policy-detail';sub.textContent=x.feature_group+' · '+x.variant+' · '+x.policy_alias;policy.append(sub);cell(tr,'Saved policy',policy);cell(tr,'2024 · 919/919',metric(x.annual_values[0],x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'2025 · 934/934',metric(x.annual_values[1],x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'Validation score',metric(x.selection_score,x.metric),'num');cell(tr,'2026 · 755/755',metric(x.annual_values[2],x.metric),'num');$('leader-rows').append(tr)}const different=rows.filter(x=>!x.same_policy_as_primary).length;text('profile-note',profile==='50/50'?'Declared primary: equal annual validation weights. 2026 is shown only as test reporting. Accuracy is higher-is-better; the other objectives are lower-is-better.':'Sensitivity '+profile+': '+different+' objective winner(s) differ from the primary. Saved annual predictions remain unchanged, with zero sensitivity refits. 2026 does not select this result.');}
$('profile').addEventListener('change',renderLeaders);renderLeaders();for(const x of s.leaders.filter(x=>x.profile==='50/50')){const tr=document.createElement('tr');cell(tr,'Objective',objective(x.target,x.metric));for(const profile of s.profiles){const row=s.leaders.find(y=>y.profile===profile&&y.target===x.target&&y.metric===x.metric);cell(tr,profile,row.primary_policy_rank,'num')} $('rank-rows').append(tr)}
const names={draftkings:'DraftKings',kalshi:'Kalshi',polymarket:'Polymarket Global',polymarket_us:'Polymarket US'},routes={the_odds_api_v4:'The Odds API',kalshi_native:'Native Kalshi',polymarket_native:'Native Polymarket',polymarket_us_native:'Native Polymarket US'};
function renderSources(){const year=Number($('source-season').value),target=$('source-target').value;const rows=d.sources.t120_completed_coverage.filter(x=>x.season===year&&x.target===target);rows.sort((a,b)=>{const order=['draftkings','kalshi','polymarket','polymarket_us'];return (order.includes(a.bookmaker)?order.indexOf(a.bookmaker):-1+100)-(order.includes(b.bookmaker)?order.indexOf(b.bookmaker):-1+100)||a.bookmaker.localeCompare(b.bookmaker)});$('source-rows').replaceChildren();for(const x of rows){const tr=document.createElement('tr');tr.dataset.bookmaker=x.bookmaker;const title=document.createElement('span');title.className='policy-name';title.textContent=names[x.bookmaker]||x.bookmaker;const sub=document.createElement('span');sub.className='policy-detail';sub.textContent=routes[x.source_route]||x.source_route;title.append(sub);cell(tr,'Bookmaker / route',title);cell(tr,'Qualified features',x.feature_qualified_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');cell(tr,'Original availability',x.strict_original_availability_qualified_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');cell(tr,'Predictive baseline',x.predictive_baseline_qualified_n+' / '+x.expected_n,'num');$('source-rows').append(tr)}text('source-note','Saved matrix: '+num(d.sources.coverage_rows)+' coverage rows, '+d.sources.bookmakers.length+' bookmakers/products and '+d.sources.horizons.length+' horizons. Source inspection '+clock(d.sources.as_of)+'; qualification boundary '+clock(d.sources.qualification_boundary)+'. This view is T-120, completed games only.');}
$('source-season').addEventListener('change',renderSources);$('source-target').addEventListener('change',renderSources);renderSources();text('exchange-note','Native exchange gaps include unbound exact-contract/source adapters, unresolved route rights and absent clock-valid quotes. Qualified replay/reference coverage is not proof of originally possessed pregame quotes, and no scored market benchmark is invented here. The current/historical qualification stages report '+d.sources.new_market_provider_requests+' new market-provider requests; that count is not a claim about every official-schedule request.');
text('next-status',n.status==='PREPARED_NOT_EXECUTED'?'Installed and native-verified · owner execution pending':'Replacement under preparation · owner execution pending');facts('next-facts',[['Planned source-ablation jobs',n.planned_source_jobs],['Additional families',n.planned_families.join(' + ')],['Completed campaign jobs to preserve',n.reuse_completed_registered_jobs],['Scientific worker target / ceiling',n.target_workers+' / '+n.worker_ceiling],['Read-only native admission',n.native_verified?n.native_admission.admitted_jobs+' / '+n.native_admission.registered_jobs:'Pending'],['Native projected workers, not measured',n.native_verified?n.native_admission.projected_workers:'Unverified'],['Checkpoint files verified unchanged',n.native_verified?n.native_admission.checkpoint_receipts_verified_unchanged:'Unverified'],['Checkpointed scoring','Parallel, resumable'],['Owner executions from preparation',n.owner_runs_launched],['Native verification',n.native_verified?'Verified '+clock(n.native_verified_at):'Not yet complete']]);text('next-digest',n.canonical_sha256?'Canonical SHA-256 '+n.canonical_sha256:'A prepared-release claim requires a sealed canonical and native verification.');text('summary-comparison','Offline comparison on the inspected '+n.summary_comparison.source_release+' summary: '+num(n.summary_comparison.original_bytes)+' → '+num(n.summary_comparison.reencoded_bytes)+' bytes after removing duplicated inline ledgers. Full stage/input pins and accountability remain preserved. This does not predict the next total scientific return size.');facts('population-facts',[['Known completed / pending games',p.completed_test_games+' / '+p.pending_test_games],['Policies scoring every known completed game',num(p.test_policies_with_full_known_completed_coverage)+' / '+num(p.test_policy_count)],['Retained market policies: pending coverage','288 policies · 123 / 133'],['Retained core policies: pending coverage','109 policies · 93 / 133'],['Official/postseason census','Completeness unproven']]);
for(const x of d.remaining_work){const row=document.createElement('div');row.className='branch';const head=document.createElement('div');head.className='branch-head';const title=document.createElement('strong');title.textContent=x.topic;const pill=document.createElement('span');pill.className='pill warn';pill.textContent=x.status.replaceAll('_',' ');head.append(title,pill);const detail=document.createElement('p');detail.textContent=x.detail;row.append(head,detail);$('remaining-branches').append(row)}
facts('storage-facts',[['Verified control ZIP',mib(d.storage.control_zip_bytes)+' · '+num(d.storage.control_zip_bytes)+' bytes'],['New separate scientific payloads',gb(d.storage.new_scientific_payload_bytes)],['New unique payloads',num(d.storage.new_unique_payloads)],['Inherited bytes not recopied',gb(d.storage.inherited_payload_bytes_not_recopied)],['Maximum transport part','512 MiB'],['Aggregate science cap','None']]);text('return-digest','Return SHA-256 '+d.storage.control_zip_sha256);for(const pin of d.evidence){const row=document.createElement('div');row.className='pin';const label=document.createElement('strong');label.textContent=pin.label+' · '+num(pin.bytes)+' bytes';const hash=document.createElement('code');hash.textContent=pin.sha256;row.append(label,hash);$('evidence-pins').append(row)}
$('download').addEventListener('click',()=>{const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify(d,null,2)+'\n'],{type:'application/json'}),url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='FBS_V097_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),2000)});text('footer-note','Evidence inspected '+clock(d.as_of)+'. Source review, website deployment, production promotion and owner research remain separate. This dated report is not a live process monitor.');
$('report').hidden=false;document.documentElement.dataset.ready='true';
})().catch(error=>{const target=document.getElementById('error');target.textContent='Evidence could not be verified: '+String(error.message||error);target.hidden=false;document.getElementById('report').hidden=true;document.documentElement.dataset.ready='error';});
</script></body></html>
